  "title": "A gold-grabbing game",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Setup Fix a tree $T$ and for every vertex $v \\in V(T)$ a non-negative integer $g(v)$ which we think of as the amount of gold at $v$.\n\n2-Player game Players alternate turns. On each turn, a player chooses a leaf vertex $v$ of the tree, takes the gold at this vertex, and then deletes $v$. The game ends when the tree is empty, and the winner is the player who has accumulated the most gold.\n\nProblem Find optimal strategies for the players.",
